==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|skilja}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*skiljaną}}, from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*(s)kelH-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈscɪlja/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɪlja|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|skildi|skilið}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|with accusative}} to [[separate]]{{jump|separate|s}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|with accusative}} to [[understand]]{{jump|understand|s}}
#: ''[[ég skil ekki|Ég '''skil''' ekki]].''
#:: [[I don't understand|I don't '''understand''']].
#: ''Fyrirgefðu, en ég '''skil''' ekki frönsku.''
#:: I'm sorry but I don't '''understand''' French.
# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[divorce]]{{jump|divorce|s}}

====Synonyms====
* {{jump|s|separate}} [[aðskilja]]
* {{jump|s|understand}} [[botna í]], [[sjá]], [[undirstanda]] (''obsolete'')
* {{jump|s|divorce}} [[slíta sambúð]]

====Derived terms====
{{der-top3}}
* {{l|is|ég skil ekki}}
* {{l|is|eiga skilinn}} (to [[deserve]] something)
* {{l|is|segja skilið við}} (to [[leave]] something, to put something behind one)
* {{l|is|skilinn}}
* {{l|is|skilja á milli}} (to [[distinguish]])
* {{l|is|skilja að}} (to divide in two)
{{der-mid3}}
* {{l|is|skilja eftir}} (to [[leave]] something, to [[leave]] something behind)
* {{l|is|skilja ekkert í}} (to be unable to understand something, make no sense of something)
* {{l|is|skilja frá}} (to separate something from something else)
* {{l|is|skilja hvað klukkan slær}}
* {{l|is|skilja mjólkina}} (to separate [[milk]] and [[cream]])
* {{l|is|skiljast}}
{{der-mid3}}
* {{l|is|skiljast að}} (to [[part]], to [[separate]])
* {{l|is|skilja sundur}} (to [[take]] apart)
* {{l|is|skilja undan}} (to make an exception of)
* {{l|is|skilja við}} (to [[die]])
* {{l|is|vera skildir að skiptum}} (to have nothing to do with someone from now on)
{{der-bottom}}

